  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1360",
      "html": "<p>Size: 120 cm SL.</p><p>Identification: Dorsum dull grey with pale green iridescence; maxillary band of teeth forms a continuous row with no break in midline. Snout protruding with upper jaw tooth bands partly exposed when mouth is closed; large median vomerine tooth plate.</p><p>Type locality: Thabo, Mekong River basin, Nongkhai Province, Thailand.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1360",
      "html": "<p>Asia: Mekong, Bangpakong and Chao Phraya basins. IUCN Red List: Least Concern (last assessed 2011).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1360",
      "html": "<p>The ultimate size of this fish, particularly when combined with its active swimming behaviour, makes it unsuitable for home aquaria.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1360",
      "html": "<p>Needs a large amount of open space for swimming room and some plants to help reduce the nervous nature of the fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1360",
      "html": "<p>Juveniles feed on prawns and insects; sub-adults and adults on prawns, insects and particularly mollusks, which are more predominant in stomach contents than in any other Pangasius species, and on plants.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1360",
      "html": "<p>Females are fuller-bodied.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1360",
      "html": "<p>Unreported. Migrates into the middle Mekong along the Thai-Lao border as water levels and turbidity begin to increase. Reproduces early in the flood season and juveniles of 6 to 7 cm are taken by late June.</p><p>There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1360",
      "html": "<p>Etymology: the name Pangasius comes from a local (Bengali) name of the fish (pungas). The name conchophilus, a combination of the Latin concho (shell) and philus (loving), refers to the pronounced molluscivory of this species. Described by Roberts &amp; Vidthayanon, 1991.</p>"
    }
  ],
